## Summary

I shipped a production-polished native Apple (**SwiftUI + MapKit**) `RouteMapSection` at full parity with `web/src/features/driving/components/drive-detail/RouteMapSection.tsx`, following the established sibling architecture (11 files: View, Model/state-holder, pure Adapter + Format ports, Views/States chrome, Previews, strings, 3 XCTest files).

**Parity reproduced:** speed-colored trail (Leaflet→MapKit `MapPolyline`, banded at 30/60/100 mph SI thresholds), start/end/anchor markers, the `hasMeaningfulRoute` stationary-GPS fallback + "Route can't be plotted" banner, the 4-band legend, start/end-time footer, FitBounds camera, and a style switcher. Bound via a P1/S8 state-holder seam (no view HTTP), P1/S10 i18n facade (every web `t()` key), P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, and all states (loading/empty/error/stale/offline/content) with VoiceOver + Dynamic Type + Reduce-Motion.

